lesson: 72
title: Some more join in: how many came, how many at first
stars: 0
explain: In a joining story we know two of three numbers: how many at first, how many came, how many at the end.
explain: If the start and the end are known, the ones that came are the end take away the start: 7 at first, 12 now, so 12 - 7 = 5 came.
explain: If the ones that came and the end are known, the start is the end take away the ones that came: 4 came, 12 now, so 12 - 4 = 8 at first.
vars: a=name b=name t=thing x=2..40 p=2..50
answer: x
exercise: {a} had {p} {t}. {b} gave {a.him} some more. Now {a} has {p+x} {t}. How many {t} did {b} give {a.him}?
exercise: There were {p} {t} in a box. {a} put some more in. Now there are {p+x} {t} in the box. How many {t} did {a} put in?
exercise: {a} had some {t}. {b} gave {a.him} {p} more. Now {a.he} has {x+p} {t}. How many {t} did {a} have at first?
exercise: There were some {t} in a bag. {a} added {p} more. Now there are {x+p} {t} in the bag. How many {t} were in the bag at first?
exercise: {a} has {p} {t}. How many more {t} does {a.he} need to get to have {p+x}?
exercise: {a} had some {t}. Then {a.he} found {p} more. Now {a.he} has {x+p}. How many {t} did {a.he} have before?
test: {a} ends up with {p+x} {t} after {b} gives {a.him} some. {a.He} started with {p}. How many {t} were given?
test: Now there are {x+p} {t} on the table, because {a} just brought {p}. How many {t} were on the table before {a} came?
test: {a} wants {p+x} {t}. So far {a.he} has collected {p}. How many {t} are still missing?
test: After getting {p} {t} from {b}, {a} counts {x+p} {t} in all. How many did {a} start with?
exercise: {a} had {p} {t}. After {b} gave {a.him} some, {a.he} had {p+x}. How many {t} did {b} give?
exercise: How many {t} did {a} have at first? {b} gave {a.him} {p} {t}, and now {a.he} has {x+p}.
exercise: {p} children were in a pool in Arizona. Some more jumped in. Now there are {p+x} children in the pool. How many jumped in?
exercise: A bus in Melbourne picked up {p} passengers at a stop and now has {x+p} passengers. Nobody got off. How many passengers were on the bus before the stop?
exercise: {a} has {p} {t}. {a.He} wants {p+x} {t} in all. How many more {t} does {a.he} need?
exercise: {a} had some {t}. {b} gave {a.him} {p.words} more, and now {a.he} has {x+p} {t}. How many did {a.he} start with?
exercise: There were {p} {t} in a basket in Ireland. {a} added some. Now the basket holds {p+x} {t}. How many {t} did {a} add?
exercise: {a} saved some dollars. Then {a.his} aunt in Ontario gave {a.him} {p} dollars. Now {a.he} has {x+p} dollars. How many dollars did {a.he} save before?
test: {p+x} ducks are on a pond in Kent after {p} more flew in. How many ducks were on the pond earlier?
test: What number must be added to {p} to get {p+x}?
test: Some {t} were in a drawer. {b} put in {p}, and the drawer then held {x+p}. How many were in the drawer to start with?
test: {a}'s team had {p} points at half time. At the end of the game it had {p+x} points. How many points did it score in the second half?
test: A library in Cardiff got {p} new books, which went on one shelf; the shelf now holds {x+p} books. How many books were on the shelf before?
test: {a} collected {p} {t} at first and then some more, finishing with {p+x}. How many {t} were in the second lot?
exercise: {a} had {p} {t}, {b} gave {a.him} some, now {a.he}'s got {p+x}. how many {b} give
exercise: some {t} in the bag, {a} adds {p}, now {x+p}. how many was there at first
exercise: {a} had {p+1} — no sorry, {p} {t}. {b} gave some, now {p+x}. how many did {b} give
exercise: {p} {t} in the box, {a} put some in, now {p+x}. Kai says {a} put in {2*p+x}. nah, how many really
test: {a}'s got {p+x} {t} now, had {p} before {b} gave some. how many {b} give
test: {a} had a few {t}, then got {p} more, now {x+p}, oh and the bag's got 2 pockets lol. how many at first
test: started with some {t}, +{p}, now {x+p}. how many at the start
exam: Whereas {a} originally held {p} {t} and, following a transfer from {b}, now holds {p+x}, determine the quantity transferred.
exam: It is given that a receptacle formerly containing {p} {t} now contains {p+x} {t}. Ascertain the number of {t} introduced in the interim.
exam: It is given that {a}, having received {p} {t} from {b}, thereby attained a holding of {p+x}. State {a}'s original holding.
exam: Determine the quantity which, when augmented by {p.words}, yields {p+x}.
exercise: {a} had {p} dollars. After {a.his} grandma passed away, {a} had {p+x} dollars, all the rest from her. How many dollars did Grandma leave {a}?
exercise: The shelter had {p} cats. More came in from families who had 'fallen on hard times', and now it has {p+x} cats. How many cats came in?
test: {b} 'borrowed' some of {a}'s {t} — nicked 'em, more like. {b} had {p}, now {b}'s got {p+x}. how many did {b} pinch
